    [releases/v0.32.0rc][MRV2][Performance] Enable Qwen CPU length optimization by default (#20327) (#20444)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Backport the same five-file Qwen feature delta from #20327
    (`ddf8e788caf3a4d719294913cfc3b0842bfe2dc9`) to `releases/v0.32.0rc`.
    Existing differences between the upstream branches are preserved.
    
    Based on upstream `ccdf1383df3debdd31fff3456b01942b509b8a60`, with one
    feature commit to preserve the current CI source/workflow snapshot.
    
    Audited Qwen3.8 Flash Next Model Runner V2 consumers automatically skip
    the redundant exact-count D2H copy and synchronized CPU mirror update.
    Exact positions, execution lengths, KV slots and accepted recurrent
    state remain device-based, following the existing paired exemption used
    by DeepSeek4.1.
    
    The capability is enabled by default without an additional-config flag
    or environment variable. AscendConfig has no changes in this PR.
    
    Eligibility is still checked once after KV initialization: exact Qwen
    model-state/native MTP types, resolved Qwen target architecture, and all
    audited QSA/GDN/PLE target and draft backend-builder pairs. Unknown
    consumers, context parallelism, sparse KV offload and realtime media
    retain exact CPU synchronization; the runner's PP guard still has
    priority. Text and ordinary non-realtime multimodal requests share this
    capability.
    
    The model state drains the previous copy stream once before enabling the
    exemption and freezes the result for its initialized lifetime. The
    shared runner receives only eight added lines for optional model-state
    initialization and capability lookup. Existing D2H producer/CPU consumer
    method bodies and unrelated models remain unchanged. QSA graph capture,
    capture-grid, sort and connector changes are outside this PR.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Yes. Eligible Qwen3.8 Flash Next MRV2 configurations use the
    synchronization optimization automatically, with no configuration
    switch. Other models keep their existing behavior. The eligibility
    guards and initialized-lifetime policy remain in place.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Eight regression functions, 21 parameterized cases, cover automatic
    initialization with no opt-in field, text/ordinary multimodal paths,
    unsupported model/speculator/target/draft consumers, DCP/PCP, sparse
    offload, realtime media, empty inventories, frozen decisions, copy
    draining and failure fallback.
    - All 21 cases passed against each checkout using the existing local
    runtime stand-ins. The new default-on initialization regression fails
    against the previous opt-in implementation. These are local stand-in
    results, not native runtime or NPU correctness results.
    - Ruff check/format, Codespell, Markdownlint CLI 0.45.0, Python
    compilation, whitespace, forbidden imports, boolean context managers,
    long-function and package-init checks passed.
    - Focused mypy checks for Python 3.10/3.11/3.12 passed for the policy,
    model state and regression test, with unavailable native imports
    skipped. The explicit missing-config fallback is retained, resolving the
    earlier CI union-attr error without reintroducing the opt-in flag.
    - Verified the same five-file feature additions on main and release,
    unchanged from the previously submitted feature delta. Existing
    branch-specific runner differences are inherited from each base;
    AscendConfig, KV connector and connector tests match their respective
    bases. The producer/consumer/eligibility methods and model state are
    preserved.
    - Refreshed the source history onto current upstream bases so CI no
    longer replays historical connector edits over the upstream
    finalize_step forwarding. The three actual connector regressions fail
    against the old main wrapper and pass against the refreshed wrapper with
    both upstream API stand-ins; the release wrapper remains passing. This
    is a local stand-in check, not a full native CPU run.
    - Native pytest collection is unavailable on this Windows host because
    Torch is absent. Full `bash format.sh ci` is unavailable because Bash is
    absent. New native CPU/full-hook CI results are pending this push.
    Earlier green CI runs validate the previous opt-in revisions, not these
    updated commits.
    - Exact-tree NPU output/cache validation and a controlled performance
    comparison for the default-on revision remain pre-merge validation.
    
    ### Checklist
    
    - [x] Automatic eligible-Qwen policy and fallback regressions.
    - [x] Same main/release feature delta; no AscendConfig or connector
    delta.
    - [x] Focused local static and stand-in checks.
    - [ ] Updated native CI and exact-tree NPU/performance validation.
    
